# Nextcloud Talk did not disassociate a deleted user from the one-to-one
# conversations they had left, so an account later created with the
# same user-id reattached to the previous holder's conversation and read its
# history (incorrect authorization by identity lifecycle, CWE-284;
# GHSA-xv6f-344w-895c, fixed in Talk 11.2.2). One-to-one rooms are keyed by
# their two participant uids -- Manager::getRoomByParticipant / room creation
# compute $name = json_encode($users) and look the room up with
# ->eq('r.name', $query->createNamedParameter($name)) -- so the uid itself is
# the join key. UserDeletedListener::handle (lib/Listener/UserDeletedListener.php:49
# at 09fdce5d) reacted to UserDeletedEvent by walking only
# $this->manager->getRoomsForUser($user->getUID()): rooms where the deleted
# user is still a participant are deleted or left to the other party, but
# one-to-one rooms the user had left keep type ONE_TO_ONE with the
# dead uid inside the JSON name, and the exact-name lookup hands them to
# whoever recycles the uid.
#
# Fix commit 75661785 (merge of PR #5633, "Reusable user ids one to one
# chats") adds Manager::getLeftOneToOneRoomsForUser(), a LIKE query over the
# same JSON name, and a second loop in handle() that rewrites each found room
# with $room->setType(Room::GROUP_CALL, true) and $room->setName(
# $user->getDisplayName(), ''); Room::setType grows a boolean escape hatch so
# the ONE_TO_ONE guard can be switched off for exactly this rewrite, and the
# system-message listener skips rooms whose old type is ONE_TO_ONE. The
# remediation is present at <fix> and absent at <fix>^.
#
# ATTENTION, rechecked. Lifecycle decision-completeness, the user-deletion
# form of the wiring family recorded across the corpus (1514, 1535, 1540,
# 1541, 1556, 1557, 1593, 1760). The defect is the absence of a second
# cleanup loop in an event handler: the vulnerable body contains no untrusted
# source (the UserDeletedEvent user is internal, not caller input), no
# dangerous sink (deleteRoom / removeUser are administrative teardown), and
# no control the fixed revision neutralises -- the change only adds work.
# Which rooms reference a dead uid is a database-schema relation (rooms the
# uid participates in vs rooms whose JSON name contains the uid), not a fact
# anywhere, so "the handler decided incompletely" is not expressible as a
# label, and a rule over labels cannot ask it.
#
# Re-measured on the real checkout against the current knowledge base,
# three --cache off runs per side, stable:
#   * lib/ (218 PHP files): 141 findings at 09fdce5d and 141 at 75661785,
#     the location-level sets identical except that the patch's inserted
#     lines move two pre-existing code.StateChangingOp marks in Manager.php
#     from :858 and :868 to :886 and :896, and one code.WeakHash in
#     Chat/SystemMessage/Listener.php from :335 to :339. Nothing fires in
#     lib/Listener/UserDeletedListener.php at either revision.
#   * the whole checkout (281 JS, 279 PHP, 368 config, 557 text-pattern
#     files): 344 findings per side, 283 at or above high, the same three
#     shifted rows the only difference.
#   * `vyql match` on lib/Listener/UserDeletedListener.php reports no
#     source, no sink and no control at either revision, and `-flags only`
#     over lib/Listener reports no review flag at either revision, so the
#     miss is not a flags-versus-findings reporting artifact.
#   * The auto-resolved analysis profile is "frontend" (the repository
#     ships package.json and webpack config beside its PHP), and a profile
#     gates source labelling by concept identity. Re-running with -profile
#     web, api and generic gives the same 141 findings and the same empty
#     listener, so no profile pruning hides a label here.
#
# The counterweights, measured rather than assumed:
#   * The documented-API route fails. The calls the fix leaves inside
#     handle() -- getLeftOneToOneRoomsForUser, setType, setName -- are the
#     application's own methods and their presence IS the remediation, not a
#     library API whose absence the code reveals: getLeftOneToOneRoomsForUser
#     exists only in the fix, and setType is called at six other places in
#     the tree at the parent (lib/Command/Room/TRoomCommand.php:134,
#     lib/Controller/RoomController.php:1085, :1202 and :1216, and
#     lib/Activity/Listener.php:154 and :199 on a different object), so a
#     `not setType` negation keys on nothing but this fix's layout and any
#     variant remediation (deleting the left rooms, a migration step,
#     checking participant existence at one-to-one creation) walks past it.
#   * A presence route cannot separate the revisions at all. The handler
#     exists at both with the same signature and the patch only adds
#     statements inside it, so labelling the handler through the
#     framework-documented OCP\User\Events\UserDeletedEvent /
#     IEventListener::handle pair fires on exactly one handler in this tree
#     (UserDeletedEvent appears in lib/AppInfo/Application.php, the
#     registration, and the listener itself; the tree carries 12
#     IEventListener::handle implementations) and fires on it identically
#     before and after the fix.
#   * The only non-additive hunk in the patch is Room::setType's guard
#     gaining !$allowSwitchingOneToOne, and an unconditional ONE_TO_ONE type
#     guard is a correct safety property rather than a defect -- flagging it
#     would fire on every immutable-type guard in every application.
#   * The fixed revision's new LIKE query parameterises and
#     escapeLikeParameter()s its input, so no injection finding is owed
#     either.
#
# No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry, as at 1760 and 1556 for this family: the missing
# piece is ontology design (a relation from a user id to the rows referencing
# it, and a lifecycle-completeness decision over that relation), not a
# localised construct in one function. No definition change ships.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-analysis-gap, real revisions both rejected

test "rank1778: the deletion handler cleans only rooms the user still participates in"
  lang php
  file lib/Listener/UserDeletedListener.php
  reject VYQL-AUTH-079
  code
  ```
  <?php

  namespace OCA\Talk\Listener;

  use OCA\Talk\Manager;
  use OCA\Talk\Room;
  use OCA\Talk\Service\ParticipantService;
  use OCP\EventDispatcher\Event;
  use OCP\EventDispatcher\IEventListener;
  use OCP\User\Events\UserDeletedEvent;

  class UserDeletedListener implements IEventListener {

  	/** @var Manager */
  	private $manager;
  	/** @var ParticipantService */
  	private $participantService;

  	public function __construct(Manager $manager,
  								ParticipantService $participantService) {
  		$this->manager = $manager;
  		$this->participantService = $participantService;
  	}

  	public function handle(Event $event): void {
  		if (!($event instanceof UserDeletedEvent)) {
  			// Unrelated
  			return;
  		}

  		$user = $event->getUser();

  		$rooms = $this->manager->getRoomsForUser($user->getUID());

  		foreach ($rooms as $room) {
  			if ($this->participantService->getNumberOfUsers($room) === 1) {
  				$room->deleteRoom();
  			} else {
  				$this->participantService->removeUser($room, $user, Room::PARTICIPANT_REMOVED);
  			}
  		}
  	}
  }
  ```

test "rank1778: the fixed revision also rewrites the one-to-one rooms the user had left"
  lang php
  file lib/Listener/UserDeletedListener.php
  reject VYQL-AUTH-079
  code
  ```
  <?php

  namespace OCA\Talk\Listener;

  use OCA\Talk\Manager;
  use OCA\Talk\Room;
  use OCA\Talk\Service\ParticipantService;
  use OCP\EventDispatcher\Event;
  use OCP\EventDispatcher\IEventListener;
  use OCP\User\Events\UserDeletedEvent;

  class UserDeletedListener implements IEventListener {

  	/** @var Manager */
  	private $manager;
  	/** @var ParticipantService */
  	private $participantService;

  	public function __construct(Manager $manager,
  								ParticipantService $participantService) {
  		$this->manager = $manager;
  		$this->participantService = $participantService;
  	}

  	public function handle(Event $event): void {
  		if (!($event instanceof UserDeletedEvent)) {
  			// Unrelated
  			return;
  		}

  		$user = $event->getUser();

  		$rooms = $this->manager->getRoomsForUser($user->getUID());
  		foreach ($rooms as $room) {
  			if ($this->participantService->getNumberOfUsers($room) === 1) {
  				$room->deleteRoom();
  			} else {
  				$this->participantService->removeUser($room, $user, Room::PARTICIPANT_REMOVED);
  			}
  		}

  		$leftRooms = $this->manager->getLeftOneToOneRoomsForUser($user->getUID());
  		foreach ($leftRooms as $room) {
  			// We are changing the room type and name so a potential follow up
  			// user with the same user-id can not reopen the one-to-one conversation.
  			$room->setType(Room::GROUP_CALL, true);
  			$room->setName($user->getDisplayName(), '');
  		}
  	}
  }
  ```

test "rank1778: one-to-one rooms are keyed by the JSON of both uids"
  lang php
  file lib/Manager.php
  reject VYQL-AUTH-079
  code
  ```
  <?php

  namespace OCA\Talk;

  use OCA\Talk\Room;
  use OCP\DB\QueryBuilder\IQueryBuilder;

  class Manager {

  	public function getRoomByParticipant(array $users): ?Room {
  		$query = $this->db->getQueryBuilder();
  		$helper = new SelectHelper();
  		$helper->selectRoomsTable($query);
  		$query->from('talk_rooms', 'r')
  			->where($query->expr()->eq('r.type', $query->createNamedParameter(Room::ONE_TO_ONE_CALL, IQueryBuilder::PARAM_INT)))
  			->andWhere($query->expr()->eq('r.name', $query->createNamedParameter(json_encode($users))));

  		$result = $query->execute();
  		$row = $result->fetch();
  		$result->closeCursor();

  		if ($row === false) {
  			return null;
  		}

  		return $this->createRoomObject($row);
  	}

  	public function getLeftOneToOneRoomsForUser(string $userId): array {
  		$query = $this->db->getQueryBuilder();
  		$helper = new SelectHelper();
  		$helper->selectRoomsTable($query);
  		$query->from('talk_rooms', 'r')
  			->where($query->expr()->eq('r.type', $query->createNamedParameter(Room::ONE_TO_ONE_CALL)))
  			->andWhere($query->expr()->like('r.name', $query->createNamedParameter('%' . $this->db->escapeLikeParameter(json_encode($userId)) . '%')));

  		$result = $query->execute();
  		$rooms = [];
  		while ($row = $result->fetch()) {
  			if ($row['token'] === null) {
  				continue;
  			}

  			$room = $this->createRoomObject($row);
  			$rooms[] = $room;
  		}
  		$result->closeCursor();

  		return $rooms;
  	}
  }
  ```
